
# Project 05 - Persistent Storage and Data Integrity

Campus Library Loan System

## Project Overview

This project explores persistent container storage and data integrity using Docker Compose, Apache HTTPD and PostgreSQL within a simulated campus library loan environment.

The project focuses on Docker named volumes, database persistence, container lifecycle management, network segmentation, resource management, container hardening and database disaster recovery.

## Technical Objectives

- Deploy Apache HTTPD and PostgreSQL containers.
- Configure CPU and memory restrictions.
- Implement frontend and backend network segmentation.
- Restrict direct database exposure.
- Configure persistent database storage using named volumes.
- Verify database records across container recreation.
- Apply least-privilege security controls.
- Perform database backup and restoration.
- Verify database record integrity after recovery.

## Service Configuration

| Parameter | Web Service | Database Service |
|---|---|---|
| Service | libraryportal | database |
| Container | library-web | library-db |
| Image | httpd:2.4 | postgres:16 |
| Published Port | 8142:80 | Disabled |
| CPU Limit | 0.55 | 0.75 |
| Memory Limit | 320 MiB | 768 MiB |
| Restart Policy | unless-stopped | always |

## Network Architecture

| Network | Driver | Connected Services |
|---|---|---|
| library-front | bridge | Web |
| library-back | bridge | Web and Database |

The database is restricted to the backend network without a published host port.

Separate frontend and backend networks reduce unnecessary service exposure while maintaining internal container connectivity.

## Docker Compose Configuration

```yaml
services:
  libraryportal:
    image: httpd:2.4
    container_name: library-web
    ports:
      - "8142:80"
    cpus: 0.55
    mem_limit: 320m
    restart: unless-stopped
    networks:
      - library-front
      - library-back
    privileged: false
    cap_drop:
      - ALL
    security_opt:
      - no-new-privileges:true

  database:
    image: postgres:16
    container_name: library-db
    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: librarydb
      POSTGRES_USER: loanuser
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD:?Set password}
    cpus: 0.75
    mem_limit: 768m
    restart: always
    networks:
      - library-back
    volumes:
      - library-data:/var/lib/postgresql/data

networks:
  library-front:
    name: library-front
    driver: bridge

  library-back:
    name: library-back
    driver: bridge

volumes:
  library-data:
    name: library-data
```

## Security Controls

| Control | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Named Docker volumes | Maintain persistent database storage |
| Volume lifecycle management | Preserve data across container recreation |
| privileged: false | Avoid privileged execution |
| cap_drop: ALL | Remove Linux capabilities |
| no-new-privileges | Prevent additional privilege acquisition |
| Network segmentation | Restrict unnecessary communication |
| Resource limits | Control resource consumption |
| Database port isolation | Reduce direct database exposure |
| Environment variables | Avoid hardcoded database passwords |

