Data persistence verification focuses on confirming that database records remain available after container recreation.

## Persistent Storage and Recovery

| Parameter | Configuration |
|---|---|
| Database | librarydb |
| Test Table | loans |
| Original Volume | library-data |
| Backup Directory | C:\LibraryBackup |
| Backup Archive | library-data.tar.gz |
| Restored Volume | library-restored |

The recovery procedure involves stopping PostgreSQL, creating a physical volume backup, restoring the archive into a separate volume and verifying the original database records.

The final Compose configuration uses library-restored as an external volume after restoration.

The original volume is retained until successful recovery has been confirmed.

## Restored Volume Configuration

Update the database service volume configuration after restoration:

```yaml
volumes:
  - library-restored:/var/lib/postgresql/data
```

Declare the restored volume at the top level:

```yaml
volumes:
  library-restored:
    name: library-restored
    external: true
```

The restored volume must exist and contain the recovered database files before deployment.

